  "question": {
    "text": "Suppose <math><mn>60</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">%</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></mrow></mrow></math> aqueous solution of glucose <math><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></math> and <math><mn>20</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">%</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></mrow></mrow></math> aqueous solution of urea <math><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></math> have equal molarity, then which solution has higher density:"
  },
